Notebook[{
Cell["Ancillary Hessian derivation (stable unit AppendixE): Mathematica 12 verification (v6 with notation revision 20260928-v3)", "Title"],
Cell["Unzip the package first. Keep this notebook next to Verify_Appendix_E.wl. Evaluate the first input cell with Shift+Enter, or choose Evaluation > Evaluate Notebook. No Python, external package, or network connection is needed.", "Text"],
Cell["The source uses exact arithmetic. The actual kernel version, check counts, and residuals are exported automatically into verification_results_v6. This notebook has no prefilled evaluation output. Save it after evaluation to retain your own result.", "Text"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Block", "[", "{", "$IterationLimit", "=", "Infinity", ",", "$ContextPath", "=", "{", "\"System`\"", "}", ",", "$Context", "=", "\"Global`\"", "}", ",", "Get", "[", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "NotebookDirectory", "[", "]", ",", "\"Verify_Appendix_E.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]"}]], "Input"],
Cell["Notation: J = Gamma(S,S), K = Delta S. JacobiMatrix denotes the matrix M_J. The old K gradient-contraction name is retained only in immutable historical records.", "Text"],
Cell["Summary", "Section"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "MergedVerificationV5`AppendixE`VerificationResults", ",", "Length", "[", "MergedVerificationV5`AppendixE`VerificationLog", "]", "}"}]], "Input"],
Cell["Every exact check", "Section"],
Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"MergedVerificationV5`AppendixE`VerificationLog", "//", "TableForm"}]], "Input"],
Cell["A success requires every expected check to run and pass, and both result files to be exported successfully. The v5 filename/context is a stable unit ID; base code release is v6, with the 20260928-v3 notation revision. Finite matrix-order tests and coordinate samples are explicitly distinguished from symbolic identities; the geometric, singular-set, spectral-domain and all-orders arguments remain in the paper.", "Text"]
}, WindowTitle -> "Ancillary Hessian derivation (stable unit AppendixE)", StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
